---
title: "RogueLike Valkur — Sequence: 60 FPS Game Frame Loop"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant L  as launcher.py
    participant G  as Game
    participant GI as GameInitializer
    participant GL as GameLoop
    participant EW as ECSWorld
    participant US as Update Systems
    participant RE as Renderer + Camera
    participant RS as Render Systems
    participant SC as pygame.Surface

    L->>G: Game(screen, perf_log, map_name)
    G->>GI: create_and_initialize()
    Note over GI: 22 stages with LoadingScreen feedback<br/>Audio · Map · ECS · Items · Editors (×8)<br/>Minimap · Renderer · Menu

    GI-->>G: initialization complete
    L->>GL: loop.run()

    loop Every frame  (target 60 FPS)
        GL->>G: handle_events()
        Note over G: pygame.event.get()<br/>ESC / resize / menu toggle

        GL->>G: update()
        Note over G: Skips ECS update if<br/>editor overlay is open

        G->>EW: update(clock, camera)
        EW->>EW: rebuild_spatial_index()  [only if dirty]
        EW->>US: run update pipeline
        Note over US: Spawner → Input → Physics → Combat<br/>Spells → AI/FSM → Inventory<br/>Experience → Chat → Audio

        US-->>EW: component mutations applied
        EW-->>G: update complete

        GL->>G: render()
        G->>RE: renderer.render_game(state, screen, camera)
        Note over RE: Map chunks · Buildings<br/>Z-layer composition

        G->>EW: render(screen, camera)
        EW->>RS: run render pipeline  (z-ordered)
        Note over RS: Entity sprites · HUD bars<br/>Spell FX · UI panels · Chat<br/>Debug overlays (DEBUG mode)

        RS-->>SC: blit calls accumulated
        RE-->>SC: pygame.display.flip()
    end

    GL->>G: shutdown()
    G->>G: flush diagnostics · stop audio · save world state
